course: dictionary
lesson: 6762
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word opera can mean a play where the actors sing, the music and theatre in general, or a building. Context clues tell you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: «Going to the opera» is about a grand night out with singing and music, so opera means the show. «A soap opera» is a long TV drama that is not sung at all, so here the word means something different. Always check the words around it.
explain: The Viking sentences show this too. «The horned helmets came from costumes for an opera in 1876» tells you the horns were costumes made for a show. They were not real battle helmets, so the context stops you believing the myth.
fact: An opera is a play in which the actors sing almost all the words, with an orchestra playing music.
fact: Opera can also mean this kind of music and theatre in general.
fact: An opera house is the building where operas are performed, such as the famous Sydney Opera House in Australia.
fact: Mozart, Verdi and Puccini are famous composers of opera.
fact: «Vikings did not wear horned helmets in battle.» The horns come from costumes made for an opera in 1876.
exercise: «Going to the opera» is a fun night out. In this sentence, what is an opera? | *A play where the actors sing almost all the words, with an orchestra | A bird that sings | A long TV drama series | A kind of helmet
exercise: «She watches every episode of her favourite soap opera.» What is a soap opera? | *A long TV drama series, not sung | An opera house by the sea | A play where all the words are sung | A famous composer
exercise: Where would you go to watch an opera being performed? | A petrol station | *An opera house | A sports field | A library
test: Which names are famous composers of opera? | *Mozart, Verdi and Puccini | Lewis Carroll and Beatrix Potter | Dr Seuss and Roald Dahl | Charles Dickens and Jane Austen
test: «He loves opera.» In this sentence, what does opera mean? | *The music and theatre in general | A petrol station | Helmets with horns | Only a building
exam: «Vikings did not wear horned helmets in battle; the horns come from costumes made for an opera in 1876.» What does this tell us? | Vikings went to the opera in 1876 | *Horned helmets were made for an opera costume, not for real Vikings | Opera costumes were always made of metal | Horned helmets were worn by Viking soldiers in battle
